      "**Underdetermined Systems ($m < n$)**:",
      "More unknowns than equations.",
      "Maximum possible rank is $\\min(m, n) = m < n$.",
      "For $AX = 0$: **ALWAYS possesses non-trivial infinitely many solutions!**",
      "For $AX = B$: Either Inconsistent (No Solution) or Infinitely Many Solutions. **NEVER has a Unique Solution!**",
      "**Overdetermined Systems ($m > n$)**:",
      "More equations than unknowns.",
      "Can be Inconsistent, Unique, or Infinitely Many depending on $\\rho(A)$ vs $\\rho([A \\vert B])$."
